{"name":"Deep Walnut","hex":"#615d58","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"deep","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Extending, reaching or positioned far from a point of reference, especially downwards.\nExtending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively.","Extending far down from the top, or surface, to the bottom, literally or figuratively."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Far, especially far down through something or into something, physically or figuratively.","In a profound, not superficial, manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/deep"},{"term":"walnut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hardwood tree of the genus Juglans.","A nut of the walnut tree."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a dark brown colour, the colour of walnut wood."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/walnut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Walnut","blocks":[{"text":"A walnut is the edible seed of any tree of the genus Juglans, most often the Persian or English walnut, Juglans regia. They are accessory fruit because the outer covering of the fruit is technically an involucre and thus not morphologically part of the carpel; this means it cannot be a drupe but is instead a drupe-like nut."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Walnuts_-_whole_and_open_with_halved_kernel.jpg/330px-Walnuts_-_whole_and_open_with_halved_kernel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walnut","wikidata":"Q208021"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg/500px-Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg/500px-Inside_of_a_walnut_in_growth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_